{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/22373-ps4-or-xbox-one","id":22373,"title":"PS4 or Xbox One?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-03T09:05:35-08:00","id":22373,"title":"PS4 or Xbox One?","content":"I need help in selecting a console for Xmas. I've been mostly an Xbox 360 user till nowI dont want to start a console war discussion, just your reasons for preferring one or the other (or both). Your advice will help me in selecting which one I'll be getting (Ive done some online research but some of the reviews do seem skewed in one direction or other).<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:39:49-08:00","id":22384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/22373-ps4-or-xbox-one#post22373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need help in selecting a console for Xmas. I've been mostly an Xbox 360 user till nowI dont want to start a console war discussion, just your reasons for preferring one or the other (or both). Your advice will help me in selecting which one I'll be getting (Ive done some online research but some of the reviews do seem skewed in one direction or other).<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general advice I've gotten on the topic is that effectively the machines are near-identical in terms of ability, and thus one should instead focus on what console-exclusive games/lines there are that you like. It doesn't matter if console X has a +5% raw computational capacity or console Y has +10% hard drive capacity, such things are fairly minor in the long run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That having been said, if you are in a position where neither one has exclusive games that you simply must have, might I suggest looking at the option of using a PC and steam? You have a slightly larger form factor, both styles of controllers are available for USB connections and with a PC you can then easily get into downloading and using game mods. This is actually what I'm considering for my next major electronics purchase, with the additional qualifier that I aim to use the high speed streaming video card sharing/streaming capabilities they're putting in the newer versions of windows to use it to also remotely run games on cheaper laptops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:43:38-08:00","id":22385,"title":"","content":"I would probably suggest a ps4 but definitely agree with what the bizarre man from canadia said. PC is probably the best platform if you don't care about exclusives. Also the PC gets loads of its own exclusives. Look at things like the Torchlight series, the Total War franchise, Most of the Might and Magic games, loads of the original and classic RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:50:53-08:00","id":22389,"title":"","content":"Between the two consoles I would go PS4, despite having been an Xbox user for years, but like the other two, I would recommend PC over both. I resisted getting a gaming PC for years, largely because I despised how snobbish some PC gamers could get, but once I gave in I was very happy with my choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T12:37:59-08:00","id":22513,"title":"","content":"Jim Sterling seems to despise the XBone somewhat more than the PS4 based on its library having so many games that have...I forget the term, but he calls it &quot;fee to pay;&quot; games that have downloadable content available from the moment of launch that you have to pay for, so you're essentially buying an incomplete game for your sixty dollars and will have to pay more to get all the missions and characters and whatnot they've already completed but are withholding from the consumer in order to get more money. I find the argument compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T15:46:52-08:00","id":22666,"title":"","content":"As a result of MS taking too long to rescind their stance on DRM, XBox has one big advantage over PS4 at the moment if you want it by Christmas.<br /> <br /> You can find them in stores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T17:18:14-08:00","id":22742,"title":"","content":"If you are already a Xbox 360 player, you might as well pick up Xbox one. Personally I would pick the PS4 because I am a PS3 player and the transition would be easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T00:32:13-08:00","id":22998,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest a WiiU?<br /> <br /> [ducks]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:06:37-08:00","id":23067,"title":"","content":"Indeed. During the last cycle I and most of my friends all had two consoles, either a PS3 or 360 and a Wii. You know why? Because it's still fun as hell when you got a bunch of friends over playing SSB, Mario Kart, Mario Party, well any Mario game with multiplayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:27:39-08:00","id":23073,"title":"","content":"Couldn't agree more on the Wii and WiiU. My friends and I love to take it in turns to lose at Punch Out Wii when we're not playing against one another at Mario Kart. As far as the two Christmas titans? I favour PS4 for it's perceived range of games (which will undoubtedly balance out as time goes on) but would seriously consider holding off for half a year or getting a PC. Hell, Valve are releasing a console at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:47:22-08:00","id":23085,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the input guys. My friends are also advising me to wait till next year and let the 'dust' settle a bit, as well as maybe the Xbox one price will drop. I just want to get peoples opinions on console preferences to help make an informed decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T07:04:53-08:00","id":23124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demetrius7997</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/22373-ps4-or-xbox-one?p=22389#post22389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the two consoles I would go PS4, despite having been an Xbox user for years, but like the other two, I would recommend PC over both. I resisted getting a gaming PC for years, largely because I despised how snobbish some PC gamers could get, but once I gave in I was very happy with my choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like PC gaming to some extent but seriously, comparing the games. Consoles just have better games overall. Consoles have a cheaper cost than PCs do if you want one that'll play as good as them. So if you are limited on money I would go with a console over a PC. That said none of the current generation has video games and they won't for at least another year. I don't count the wii u part of the current gen. It was basically a mini-step up and it is currently struggling and partially because it just has Nintendo games and I could rail on it more but I won't. If you want a nintendo box then you'll probably like it but if you want something more than it'll be a waste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:48:26-08:00","id":23178,"title":"","content":"Well, there are also the Steam boxes that are starting to come out.<br /> My reaction was pretty much this<br /> &quot;Powered by Steam&quot; Yes<br /> &quot;Cool new controller&quot; Okay, good...<br /> &quot;Full screen, system does everything the other systems do&quot; Excellent keep it coming...<br /> &quot;Running on all PC hardware for easy upgrade/replacement&quot; Awesome! That's perfe....<br /> &quot;Runs all the games that have been ported to run on linux&quot; ... And that killed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T09:24:07-08:00","id":23189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/22373-ps4-or-xbox-one?p=23178#post23178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are also the Steam boxes that are starting to come out.<br /> My reaction was pretty much this<br /> &quot;Powered by Steam&quot; Yes<br /> &quot;Cool new controller&quot; Okay, good...<br /> &quot;Full screen, system does everything the other systems do&quot; Excellent keep it coming...<br /> &quot;Running on all PC hardware for easy upgrade/replacement&quot; Awesome! That's perfe....<br /> &quot;Runs all the games that have been ported to run on linux&quot; ... And that killed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are also going to be more expensive than a console looking at the specs. The problem with Steam box is that it's trying to compete with PCs not with consoles because it can't reliably do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T10:30:21-08:00","id":23218,"title":"","content":"It is somewhat amusing for me that one of the arguments in favor of the PS4 is the price being $100 less. It so happens that here in Brazil the Xbox One is being built locally, while the PS4s are all imported. As a result, the Brazilian taxes being the absurd thing they are, the XBox One costs about the equivalent of 965 dollars (which is already ridiculous) while a PS4 costs about 1680 dollars!<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm currently upgrading my PC instead of getting a console. If I had more money to spend I'd likely wait a while to see which console ends up having more exclusives I like and get that one along with the improved PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T19:46:03-08:00","id":23463,"title":"","content":"I got a gaming laptop over the summer and was pleasantly surprised by the number of good free to play games out there. Sure there are micro transactions if you want to pay them but the games I've been playing don't require them. As for consoles, I'm waiting to see if M$ releases a special edition bundle when they release Halo 5 next year, then I might consider getting the Xbone. Otherwise I'm out of the console business for a while. If you are looking for a decent gaming laptop I wholeheartedly recommend the Lenovo Y510p with the dual GT755m and 16gb RAM setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:14:21-08:00","id":23882,"title":"","content":"PS4 for me. Mostly because I've enjoyed Sony for a few years, though I've played my brother's 360 and original Xbox a lot as well. But basically the main reason I'm going with the PS4 is because it's cheaper. And saving money is good...means I can buy more rpg things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/918-geeklord1","name":"geeklord1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar918_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T18:40:24-08:00","id":24100,"title":"","content":"I'd totally recommend a gaming PC over either choice...<i>if </i>I weren't currently dealing with yet <i>another</i> incident in which a game I bought just refuses to work as advertised.<br /> <br /> When you're not having problems, PC gaming is (I would argue) probably the most powerful and versatile platform available. But playing on console means you never have to go digging through forums and tweaking poorly-understood parameters to get results. Pick whichever box gets you the platform-exclusive titles you want, and provided your machine doesn't pull any red-ring-of-death stuff, you're golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T20:24:06-08:00","id":24145,"title":"","content":"By the same token, if a console game is fucked up, there's no fix for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T07:07:15-08:00","id":24341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/22373-ps4-or-xbox-one?p=24145#post24145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, if a console game is fucked up, there's no fix for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are patches now. Unless the developer is a dick about it. The only time this has been an issue, (Because Developers can't afford to be this lazy on consoles) is with Skyrim and Fallout which are both made by the same company and each patch seemingly adds more bugs per fix. Other times I haven't noticed an issue. The only other time when there have been bugs have been on a few notable 3ds games.<br /> <br /> Another issue with PCs is optimization there are a number of games that have been poorly optimized on PC compared to a Console. While that means that PC's can still run it better. The quality of your system has to be significantly higher. Playing a game like Metro last light on a console to the point where it's better leagues better than the PS3/Xbox version, requires an extremely expensive computer. This doesn't happen with all games but when it happens it sucks. Console games have had this issue before but it's not as frequently occurring because developers can't just put in a Slider and have you adjust the graphics and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 12-06-2013, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:33:36-08:00","id":24430,"title":"","content":"Going on what Epimetheus said, I still have not played Fallout New Vegas because of the bugs on the 360, by time it was fixed I was a few games past it. A friend gave me a copy when he worked for Bethesda so I'm eventually going back to it, but I have so many games to play because of the new laptop it's not a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:14:44-08:00","id":24593,"title":"","content":"XBox One for me, but I will eventually be getting a PS4 as well. I live in a multi-platform household. PS2 &amp; 3, Xbox 360, Wii, PCs, Laptops, tablets, and the various phones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T20:35:37-08:00","id":30246,"title":"","content":"I personally belong to the &quot;Wait a year&quot; camp.<br /> News I've seen says that 1 in 250 PS4s end up doing the &quot;Blue Line of Death&quot; within a few days of set up (though any that don't brick in the first couple days seem to be fine), and a similar or slightly larger percentage of Xbones will suddenly experience catastrophic disc drive failures (there are plenty of youtube videos, they tend to sound like golf balls in a blender...).<br /> <br /> Give them a year and they will A&gt; work out the initial mechanical/circuit problems B&gt; drop the price $100-$200 C&gt; bundle a controller and a game with the system, and D&gt; possibly offer a new color choice for the console.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T06:17:47-08:00","id":30392,"title":"","content":"I'd wait until the PS4 comes out with its inevitable 4.1 model, or whatever they call those things. Everyone I know who's ever bought the original hardware of a given Playstation generation has seen the machine die and need replacement, while I've always bought the newer, smaller, sleeker model and never had any trouble from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:19:07-08:00","id":30432,"title":"","content":"PS4 is the go-to for console MMOs, and since my new job is to write about MMOs (I'm sure I'll tire of mentioning that eventually) that's the console I'm getting. Eventually. PC is fine for now though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1415-nonsensicles","name":"Nonsensicles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}